  "name": "Sound Collage",
  "family": "electronic",
  "lineage": "Running from Cage's Imaginary Landscape No. 5 (1952) and the Buchanan-Goodman break-in records through the Residents, Negativland, John Oswald's Plunderphonics (1985) and the tape-trading underground, it assembles finished music into new work by splice, turntable, sampler and radio capture — abrupt cuts between unrelated sources, recognizable fragments left legible, speech and broadcast material foregrounded, and no continuous metre unless a host loop imposes one.",
